<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15436" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕlĕgīa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕlĕgēa</span></b> , in Ov. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕlĕgēĭă</span></b> ),
			ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλεγεία</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An elegy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">form elegia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 10, 1, 58</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">93</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 1,
				2, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 5, 30, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Aus. Parent. 7, 1</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">form elegea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					1, 8, 6</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">form elegeia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 3, 1, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 9, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. R. Am.
			379</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A kind of reed</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">est et obliqua harundo, non in excelsitatem
					nascens, sed juxta terram fruticis modo se spargens,
					suavissima in teneritate animalibus: vocatur a quibusdam
					elegia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 36, 66, § 167</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
